<p>A short is seen on a phone before it plays, so the person fills the frame and the words sit at the foot, big, where a thumb does not cover them. The note in the hand goes top right.</p>
<div class="frame-preview" style="--fw: 1080; --fh: 1920; max-width: 24rem"><iframe src="/frames/thumb-short/" title="thumb-short" loading="lazy"></iframe></div>
<p class="im-cluster"><a class="im-btn im-btn-sm" href="/frames/thumb-short/">Open at 1080 × 1920 {{icon "arrow-up-right"}}</a><span class="im-hint"><code>im-studio-thumb-short</code></span></p>
<p>Change the words in <code>site/pages/frames/thumb-short.hbs</code> and export with <code>npm run frames thumb-short</code>; or rebuild it as layers with <a href="/content-creation/youtube/pixelmator/">the Pixelmator script</a>. The person is <code>demo.me</code> — the owner’s portrait in <code>assets/brand/</code> — and <code>--im-studio-focus</code> on the person says which part of the photograph to keep.</p>
